light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">## Proof</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">Apply function extensionality and the square-zero law of Definition 1.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">## Description</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">An extensional reformulation of the square-zero law using library function composition.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">namespace</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Fixture2000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/-- **Bridge for Definition 1** (Fixture2000). Function extensionality converts the pointwise square-zero law into an equality of functions. -/</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">theorem</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> differential_comp_zero</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (c : ChainComplexToy) (n : Nat) :</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    Function.comp (c.differential n) (c.differential (n + </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)) = </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> _ => </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> := </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">by</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  funext x</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  exact c.square_zero n x</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">end</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Fixture2000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>",
    "source_text": "import HomAlg.Fixture2000.Def_1\n\n/-!\n```yaml node\n{\n  \"id\": \"Fixture2000.Bridge_Def_1_mathlib\",\n  \"kind\": \"lemma\",\n  \"doc\": \"Fixture2000\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"chapter\": \"1\",\n    \"section\": \"1.1\",\n    \"label\": \"Bridge for Definition 1\",\n    \"pages\": [\n      1\n    ]\n  },\n  \"title\": \"Bridge for Definition 1\",\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"chain-complex\",\n    \"bridge\"\n  ],\n  \"concepts\": {\n    \"defines\": [],\n    \"uses\": []\n  },\n  \"deps\": {\n    \"statement\": [\n      \"Fixture2000.Def_1\"\n    ],\n    \"proof\": []\n  },\n  \"decls\": [\n    \"Fixture2000.differential_comp_zero\"\n  ],\n  \"fidelity\": {\n    \"status\": \"faithful\"\n  },\n  \"nl_proof_source\": {\n    \"follows\": \"agent\"\n  },\n  \"aux\": {\n    \"parent\": \"Fixture2000.Def_1\",\n    \"kind\": \"bridge\",\n    \"reason\": \"Relate the pointwise source formulation to library function composition.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Statement\n\nThe composite of consecutive differentials of a toy chain complex is the constant zero function.\n\n## Proof\n\nApply function extensionality and the square-zero law of Definition 1.\n\n## Description\n\nAn extensional reformulation of the square-zero law using library function composition.\n-/\n\nnamespace Fixture2000\n\n/-- **Bridge for Definition 1** (Fixture2000). Function extensionality converts the pointwise square-zero law into an equality of functions. -/\ntheorem differential_comp_zero (c : ChainComplexToy) (n : Nat) :\n    Function.comp (c.differential n) (c.differential (n + 1)) = fun _ => 0 := by\n  funext x\n  exact c.square_zero n x\n\nend Fixture2000\n"
